=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed existing widgets: WidgetShell, types.ts, registry.ts (telemetry category at lines 730-752).
Hooks: useSignalStats (signal count/oldest/newest), useSignalGaps (live signals map), useSignals (available signals list).
Types: SignalStats {vehicleId, count, oldest, newest}, gapData returns Record<string, {value, timestamp}>.
Pattern reference: MQTTStatusWidget, LiveSignalsWidget — both use WidgetShell freshness props.

=== REASONING ===
Widget computes:
- totalSignals: from useSignals catalog length
- activeCount / staleCount: iterate useSignalGaps entries, classify by 5-min threshold
- freshnessAge: seconds since newest timestamp in live data
- gapSignals: sorted list of stale/missing signals for wide view

Layouts:
- Compact (cols<=1): centered badge ratio, total count, freshness age
- Standard (2×4): 2×2 grid of StatCards (Total, Active, Gaps, Freshness) + health badge
- Wide (3×4+): adds scrollable stale signal list with last-seen times

Health color coding: green (0% stale), amber (>0% but <50%), red (>=50%).
All strings via useTranslation('dashboard'). Null-safe throughout.

